;;; Commentary:

;; Written for Emacs in yaft on a reMarkable 2 (via tmux/mosh).
;;
;; What that display path can actually show, from yaft's screen.cpp:
;;   - each cell colour is reduced to a brightness, then to one of three
;;     tones: Black (<= 85), Dither (86..169, a checkerboard), White (>= 170);
;;   - cells are painted with the A2/DU waveforms, which are 1-bit, so the
;;     checkerboard is the only "grey" that survives a partial redraw;
;;   - attributes: bold (a bold glyph), underline (fg/bg swapped on the last
;;     pixel row), reverse. No italic, no dim, no blink worth using.
;;
;; So this theme uses exactly: default black-on-white, GREY (#808080 ->
;; dither) for de-emphasis, bold for emphasis, underline for links and
;; matches, reverse for the current line / selection / mode line.
;; It sets only `t' specs, so it is the same everywhere; init.el loads it
;; only when `display-graphic-p' is nil.


